From: tiansin <tiansin@tiansin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] compile: preserve builtin error wrapper with runtime obfuscation

The runtime must emit the error.Error method wrapper even when imported
packages already mention the error type. Compare the canonical package
path so this exception still applies when runtime has been obfuscated.
---
 cmd/compile/internal/noder/reader.go | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/cmd/compile/internal/noder/reader.go b/cmd/compile/internal/noder/reader.go
--- a/cmd/compile/internal/noder/reader.go
+++ b/cmd/compile/internal/noder/reader.go
@@ -4008,7 +4008,7 @@
 	}
 
 	// Special case: runtime must define error even if imported packages mention it (#29304).
-	forceNeed := typ == types.ErrorType && base.Ctxt.Pkgpath == "runtime"
+	forceNeed := typ == types.ErrorType && base.TranslateGarblePkgPath(base.Ctxt.Pkgpath) == "runtime"
 
 	// If a type was found in an imported package, then we can assume
 	// that package (or one of its transitive dependencies) already
